-- title:
--   Crossing two auxiliary data at a prescribed automorphism
-- statement:
--   Let $L/K$ be a Galois extension of number fields whose Galois group $L \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]} L$ is commutative, let $\mathfrak f$ be an ideal of $\mathcal O_K$ and let $\sigma$ be an element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$. The index set is `primeCarriers K 𝔣`, the set of those elements of the group of carriers coprime to $\mathfrak f$ that are of the form `primeUnit K v` for a finite place $v$ of $K$ with $v \nmid \mathfrak f$. Assume given, for each such carrier $i$, a datum $D_i$ of type `ArtinFieldCore K L 𝔣 i` (auxiliary fields $E_i \subseteq N_i$ and $\Theta_i$ over $K$ together with a modulus $\mathfrak m_i$ divisible by $\mathfrak f$, a place $w$ of $E_i$ above $v$ of residue degree $1$, and a primitive $q$-th root of unity generating $\Theta_i$ over $E_i$), and for each ordered pair $(i,j)$, including $i=j$, a datum $P_{ij}$ of type `ArtinPairCore K L 𝔣 σ (D i) (D j)`: a common layer $N''_{ij}/E''_{ij}$ dominating $E_i$ and $E_j$, with a modulus $\mathfrak m''_{ij}$ divisible by $\mathfrak f$, $\mathfrak m_i$ and $\mathfrak m_j$, such that `modulusExt K E'' 𝔪''` is an admissible modulus for $N''/E''$, the Artin symbol of $K$-carriers obtained by relative norm from $E''$ agrees with the restriction of the Artin symbol of $N''/E''$, the restriction homomorphism `resHom K L E'' N''` is injective and has $\sigma$ in its range. Assume moreover that for every pair $(i,j)$ and every intermediate field $F$ of $N''_{ij}/E''_{ij}$ with $[F:E''_{ij}]$ prime, the predicate `IdeleFirstIneqData` holds for $F$ over $E''_{ij}$ at the modulus `modulusExt K E'' 𝔪''`, i.e. there is a homomorphism $\mathrm{Nrm}$ of idele unit groups carrying adjusters to adjusters of the relative norm, compatible with the content homomorphism and the relative norm on fractional-ideal units, whose range contains the unit ideles when the modulus is admissible, and with $[F:E'']$ dividing the index of the subgroup generated by the principal ideles and the range of $\mathrm{Nrm}$. The conclusion is that for every ordered pair $(i,j)$ of carriers there exist $b$ in the carrier group $(D_i).\mathrm{Ip}$ of $E_i$ coprime to `modulusExt K E_i 𝔪_i`, and $b'$ in the corresponding group for $D_j$, with equal images under the relative-norm maps $(D_i).\mathrm{Ni}$ and $(D_j).\mathrm{Ni}$ into the carriers of $K$ coprime to $\mathfrak f$, and with $(D_i).\omega\mathrm{pi}\,b = \sigma$; no condition is imposed on the symbol of $b'$, and the witnesses depend on the pair.
--
--   This is the crossing step in Artin's proof of the reciprocity law: the auxiliary data attached to two primes are compared inside a common layer, where the first inequality on the prime-degree subextensions yields an element of the first datum realising the prescribed automorphism whose norm is simultaneously a norm from the second datum. It feeds the statements that the Artin symbol is surjective with kernel the norm ray subgroup, and the construction of transfer data in degree three.
